{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310760,"nonce":"fOlrO4ejXcMtWwmMcFaKQdeKm5A=","title":"2026-07-06 cluster: FIVE x-module resolution failures found landing the flash port, all one root family (declared types lost at call/field ...","message":"`runtime_mapping::class_matches` (408) matched exact / `_`-suffix only, so a bare `PrefillGraph`\nlookup missed the DOT-registered `nue.engine.PrefillGraph` → fell to a name-only path that\ncollapsed same-name+arity externs onto the first candidate (nue.engine.PrefillGraph.bucketFor →\nBertGraph's symbol → 0 → graph silently disabled). FIX = add `registered.ends_with(\".{lookup}\")`\n(dot analog of the `_` rule). Detail in [[project_llama_prefill_graph]]. LESSON: this collapse is\nNOT namespace-gated — relocating rayzor.ds→nue.engine did NOT fix it (I mis-claimed it did). Still\nOPEN general root: primary call path (hir_to_mir.rs:17512) uses raw `get_function_id`, find_by_name\nignores arity.\n\nBodyless `@:native` extern methods were registered `return_type: 3 // PtrVoid` hardcoded → scalar\nreturns (`:Int`/`:Bool`/`:Float`) decay to a boxed pointer → null in string-concat / garbage as a\nhandle (raw i64 fine for compares/arith). FIXED: `haxe_type_to_native_tag` maps the real declared\ntype into the native-tag scheme (0=Void 1=I64 2=F64 3=PtrVoid 4=Bool — NOT `haxe_type_to_descriptor`'s\n3=I32/9=Ptr scheme). Params still PtrVoid (ride `external_function_param_types`). Detail +\nsame-name-collapse-fixed-by-relocation in [[project_llama_prefill_graph]]. STILL OPEN (general\nroot): primary static-call path hir_to_mir.rs:17512 uses raw `get_function_id` (SymbolId, drifts\nx-module) not `resolve_function_id_with_qualified_fallback`:1618; `find_by_name` (runtime_mapping.rs:338)\nfirst-match ignores arity; `class_matches`:408 suffix-matches; NO `external_function_return_types` map.\n\nServer SIGSEGV'd in nue.Linear.forward at first request. TWO cluster shapes at once, BOTH\nsilently accepted by the compiler: (1) CausalLanguageModel-cast value passed where GenerationLoop\ndeclares concrete LlamaModel → iface fat-ptr read as object → 0x001f… tag-garbage pointer deref;\n(2) local `class LocalTempSampler` inside server Main.hx duplicating nue.sampling.LocalTempSampler\nby NAME, instance passed Sampler-typed into the loop's concrete LocalTempSampler slot (same-name\ncollapse → null deref once shape 1 was fixed). Fix = port server to llama-chat's concrete shapes\n(shared LocalTempSampler, concrete LlamaModel, no iface on hot path); verified 73 tok/s, bench 1/1\nok. THE COMPILER BUG remains: both shapes should be hard type errors. DEBUG TECHNIQUE for MAP_JIT\ncrashes (lldb cannot attach): read ~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/rayzor-*.ips for the faulting\nPC, rerun with RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1, nearest fn-ptr ≤ PC names the crashing JIT fn + offset.\n\n\nAll found in ONE session wiring nue.transformer.{Q8Cache,FlashDecode} into KVCache/GQAttention.\nOne root family: the tast loses DECLARED types (fields, extern returns, same-package classes) and\nfalls into silent dynamic/Float/stub paths instead of hard-failing. Worked around in kernel code\n(each site commented); root fix = continue 2c879257 declaration-based signature resolution +\nextend E0801-style hard-fail to EVERY unresolved-receiver outcome (feedback_no_silent_dispatch_fallthrough).\n\n1. **Extern-return Float decay**: `var dBase = data.address()` (field-loaded receiver chain) —\n   return type Usize silently becomes Float; `dBase + Usize.fromInt(n)` lowers as FP ADD -\u003e\n   SIGSEGV with float-bit-pattern fault address (0x42xxxxxx00000000 shape). `.raw()` (ambiguous\n   name) correctly E0801s; `.address()` (unique name) silently decays. Workaround: `:Usize`\n   annotations on every address local.\n2. **Conditional-int-reassign Float decay (MIR)**: `if (q2 == 0x400) { q2 = 0; e += 1; }` then\n   read -\u003e q2/e decay to Float, function returns f32 BIT PATTERN as Int. stealLoop family\n   (c33c25ab) — still unfixed at root. Data-dependent (fired only on scales just below powers of\n   2 = mantissa carry). Workaround: branchless arithmetic-carry f16 encoder in Q8Cache.\n3. **Same-package implicit resolution fails x-module**: KVCache (nue.transformer) calling\n   nue.transformer.Q8Cache methods WITHOUT `import nue.transformer.Q8Cache` -\u003e method bodies\n   never link, calls hit [safety-net:fwdref-stub] -\u003e SIGTRAP exit 133. Explains the pre-existing\n   explicit `import nue.transformer.KvCacheQ8;` in KVCache. Workaround: explicit imports.\n4. **Haxe method returning extern class stubs x-module**: Q8Cache.dequantRows(len):Tensor -\u003e\n   fwdref-stub even with imports wrong?? (observed pre-import-fix; possibly same as #3 — NOT\n   re-isolated after the import fix landed. Re-test before chasing.) Workaround anyway:\n   dequantInto(len, out:Tensor):Void fill-into shape (params resolve; append proved it).\n5. **Cross-class same-name collapse**: KVCache had keysQ8.dequantView (extern KvCacheQ8) AND\n   keysQ8H.dequantView (Haxe Q8Cache) -\u003e cranelift \"can't resolve symbol dequantView\" panic\n   (bare method name emitted as symbol). Also the reason the pre-rename code ACCIDENTALLY ran:\n   unique-vs-extern-row name coincidence steered dispatch. Workaround: distinct name.\n+ **enabled()-in-ctor garbage-true**: FlashDecode.enabled() (x-module static w/ Sys.getEnv)\n   called from KVCache ctor returned true with env UNSET -\u003e both A/B arms silently ran the guest\n   path (fake 0.0000-dlogit \"parity\"). Workaround: env read in LlamaArch (proven site), threaded\n   as explicit ctor param.\n\n- `RAYZOR_DUMP_TOPK=1` in llama-chat Main.hx: per-step top-5 `id:logit`. A/B validated the port:\n  prefill logits IDENTICAL plugin-vs-guest (byte-parity of quantize), first divergence exactly at\n  first flash step, max|dlogit|=0.53@33 steps, argmax 33/33. USE THIS for any future kernel A/B.\n\nEditing `nue/nue/Q4Matmul.hx` repeatedly breaks field resolution in UNRELATED modules.\nTWO distinct triggers seen, so the earlier \"hoist the static inline var\" workaround is NOT\nthe general fix:\n  T1: a closure referencing a class-level `static inline var`\n  T2: changing two helper signatures Bytes -\u003e Usize + hoisting `bsums.address()`\nSymptom both times: `E0100 Cannot access field 'X': class not registered or field does not\nexist` — first on `LlamaArch.hx:173` `model.spinPool` (a LlamaModel field), then ALSO on\n`Q4Matmul.dumpCensus`, i.e. the whole module stopped registering.\n\n**THE COMPILER HAS A BUILT-IN DIAGNOSTIC: `RAYZOR_E0100_DEBUG=1`** (emission site\ncompiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs:~28905). It prints field / sym / receiver_ty / kind. Output:\n  field='dumpCensus' sym=SymbolId(6293) receiver_ty=TypeId(907)\n    kind=Some(\"Class { symbol_id: SymbolId(6276), type_args: [] }\")\n  ... same shape for spinPool, cache, fromQuant, floatToI32, i32ToFloat, doubleToI64,\n      i64ToDouble; plus fastCodeAt with receiver_ty=TypeId(4294967295) (INVALID).\n\n**ROOT CAUSE IS NOW PINNED: the CLASS resolves fine (receiver_ty is a valid\n`Class{symbol_id}`) — it is the FIELD lookup BY SymbolId that misses.** Classic SymbolId\ndrift. Failures cluster on STATICS (dumpCensus/fromQuant/floatToI32/i32ToFloat/doubleToI64)\nplus instance fields (spinPool/cache).\n\n**FIX DIRECTION (matches every prior fix in this cluster — resolve by NAME):** at the E0100\nsite, before `add_error`, recover the symbol via the existing name-keyed map\n`class_method_by_name: BTreeMap\u003c(SymbolId, InternedString), SymbolId\u003e` (hir_to_mir.rs:433,\nalready used this way at :1585, :11016, :11118, :12816) keyed by (receiver class symbol,\nfield name), and retry. NOTE: recovering the symbol is only half of it — the failing path is\nINSTANCE-FIELD-ACCESS lowering, so statics like `dumpCensus` need routing to the static/method\npath, not the field path. Do not land this without verifying, an unverified symbol-resolution\nchange produces silent miscompiles rather than honest errors.\n\nBLAST RADIUS: this gates the whole Tensor/QTensor -\u003e Haxe port. Every kernel edit is a coin\nflip on an unrelated module failing to resolve. Fix this BEFORE more kernel work.\nWIP blocked on it: /tmp/Q4Matmul.q6k-capture-wip.hx (Q6_K capture-set fix, worth ~10%).\nAt the E0100 site (hir_to_mir.rs ~28905) I added a fallback before `add_error`:\n  ATTEMPT 1: class by SymbolId (`class_instance_fields.get(\u0026class_sym)` where class_sym came\n             from receiver_ty's `Class{symbol_id}`) + field by NAME.  -\u003e STILL FAILS.\n             Proves the CLASS SymbolId drifts too, not just the field's. A name-based field\n             lookup behind an id-based class lookup is still an id-based resolution.\n  ATTEMPT 2: class by NAME (scan class_instance_fields matching the class symbol's NAME) +\n             field by NAME.  -\u003e STILL FAILS.\n=\u003e **Most likely conclusion: `class_instance_fields` DOES NOT CONTAIN these classes in this\nlowering context at all.** LlamaModel is lowered in another module; if its field table is\nnever forwarded, NO lookup strategy against that map can work. The map is not stale, it is\nABSENT. Note the `type_table` DOES have the class (diagnostic shows a valid\n`Class{symbol_id}`) — so the TYPE crosses the module boundary but its FIELD LAYOUT does not.\n=\u003e REAL FIX DIRECTION: forward cross-module class field tables into the consuming context\n(or resolve fields against whatever registry the type_table's Class entry can reach), rather\nthan patching the resolution strategy at the access site. VERIFY THE MAP CONTENTS FIRST —\ninstrument the fallback to print whether the class name was found and dump the keys of\nclass_instance_fields; do not attempt a third strategy blind.\nBoth attempts were REVERTED (unverified compiler edits on the field-access path for every\nclass in every program are a silent-miscompile risk, strictly worse than the loud failure).\n`RAYZOR_E0100_DEBUG=1` now also prints class-name / in_cif_by_id / in_cif_by_name / cif_len.\nOne instrumented run settled what two blind fixes could not:\n  field='spinPool' receiver_ty=TypeId(947) kind=Class{symbol_id: SymbolId(7502)}\n    class_name=Some(\"LlamaModel\") in_cif_by_id=false in_cif_by_name=false **cif_len=0**\n**`class_instance_fields` is EMPTY in the lowering context that resolves the access.** Not\nstale, not keyed differently — ABSENT. So NO resolution strategy at the access site can ever\nwork, which is exactly why both attempts failed (id-keyed class, then name-keyed class).\nThe class itself is fine: it resolves to a valid `Class{symbol_id}` and its NAME recovers\ncleanly. **The TYPE crosses the module boundary; the FIELD LAYOUT does not.**\nThe error text \"class not registered or field does not exist\" is MISLEADING — the class IS\nregistered.\n**FIX BELONGS UPSTREAM:** populate/forward `class_instance_fields` (and whatever the static\npath uses for `dumpCensus`) into the consuming context BEFORE field-access lowering runs, or\npoint resolution at a registry that survives the boundary the way `type_table` does. Do not\nadd another access-site fallback.\nLESSON: I wrote two fixes on the same unverified assumption before instrumenting. The probe\ncost one build and produced a definitive answer. Instrument BEFORE the second attempt, always.\n`class_instance_fields` has exactly ONE writer: `register_class_metadata`\n(hir_to_mir.rs:39565, insert at :40154), called only from `register_type_metadata`\n(:39306), which is driven by ONE loop over **`hir_module.types`** (:2743-2747).\nSo the map is populated ONLY for types present in `hir_module.types` for THAT context.\nMeasured `cif_len=0` at the failing access means that collection had **NO classes at all** —\nnote this is stronger than \"imported classes are missing\": even LlamaArch's OWN declarations\n(the file where the error is reported, LlamaArch.hx:173) are absent. So either\n  (a) the failing field-access lowering runs in a context/pass that never saw ANY type decls\n      (per-function context? whole-program merge pass?), or\n  (b) it runs BEFORE the registration loop at :2743.\nNEXT STEP: print at the E0100 site which module/context is being lowered and whether\n`register_type_metadata` has run yet (e.g. a counter incremented in register_class_metadata,\ndumped alongside cif_len). That distinguishes (a) from (b) in one run. THEN fix ordering or\nforward the tables — do NOT add another access-site fallback (two already failed; the map is\nempty, so no lookup strategy can work).\nProbe output across 69 failure sites, Qwen Q6_K run:\n  class_name=Some(\"LlamaModel\") in_cif_by_id=false in_cif_by_name=false\n  cif_len=0 type_meta_calls=1 cur_fn=Some(IrFunctionId(4))\n  (also Q4Matmul, FPHelper, and class_name=None; 63x type_meta_calls=1, 6x =2)\nREAD: registration DID run in these contexts (1-2 types) but registered ZERO CLASSES, and\nthe contexts carry very low IrFunctionIds. **The field access is lowered in a context that is\nneither the class's declaring module nor the obvious referencing module** — it holds a couple\nof non-class type decls and has NO class field tables. `class_instance_fields` is PER-CONTEXT\nand never shared, so LlamaModel's layout does not exist where the access is resolved. Class\nNAMES still resolve (symbol_table crosses fine); only the LAYOUT is missing.\nRULES OUT: (1) both access-site fallbacks I tried (id-keyed and name-keyed) — the map is\nempty, no strategy works; (2) the simpler \"imported classes aren't registered\" story — even a\nLOCAL class would be missing from these contexts.\n**FIX DIRECTION: class field metadata must come from a WHOLE-PROGRAM registry shared across\nlowering contexts, not each context's own `hir_module.types`** (single writer chain:\nregister_class_metadata :39565 insert :40154 \u003c- register_type_metadata :39306 \u003c- loop over\nhir_module.types :2743). Start by finding what creates these small contexts (low\nIrFunctionIds, 1-2 types) — that identifies the pass that needs the shared registry.\nAdded a process-global `CLASS_FIELD_LAYOUTS: OnceLock\u003cMutex\u003cHashMap\u003cString, Vec\u003c(String,u32)\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e`\npublished from register_class_metadata's insert site, consumed at the E0100 access site\n(name-keyed, GEP-index-only — TypeIds are per-context and must not travel). STILL E0100, and\nthe probe shows why: **`GLOBAL registry: 0 classes` at failure time — the publish site has\nrun for ZERO classes in the whole process by then.** Since unedited programs DO resolve\nfields (layouts get registered eventually in some context), the surviving hypothesis is\n**ORDERING: the failing module lowers BEFORE any class-registering context runs.**\nFirst-writer-wins cannot help when the writer has not run yet.\nIN FLIGHT: `[reg-class]` trace inside register_class_metadata (prints every execution with\nclass name, behind RAYZOR_E0100_DEBUG) interleaved with the E0100 failures — /tmp/order.log.\nIf reg-class count is 0 for the entire run: classes are registered by a DIFFERENT path than\nregister_class_metadata in this pipeline (find it: grep class_instance_fields reads at\n:19791/:30201/:30328/:30501 work in normal runs — where does their data come from?). If\nreg-class events exist but all come AFTER the failures: pure ordering — fix = topological\nmodule order, or LAZY on-demand layout computation at the access site from symbol_table/\ntype_table (the class symbol resolves fine there; check whether member symbols are reachable\nfrom it to compute GEP indices without the declaring context).\nUncommitted working-tree state: registry+probes in compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs (3 probes:\ncif-state, type_meta_calls+cur_fn committed at 3ea9a164/19eae55b; registry+reg-class trace\nUNCOMMITTED). Q6_K capture WIP still at /tmp/Q4Matmul.q6k-capture-wip.hx.\n`[reg-class]` entry trace: register_class_metadata RUNS for 88 classes incl. LlamaModel\n(twice, two contexts, log lines 629+809), interleaved with spinPool failures at 525/711/891\n— so failure #3 happens AFTER registration, yet the global registry read 0 AT EVERY failure.\n=\u003e My publish (next to `class_instance_fields.insert` at ~:40154) NEVER EXECUTES even though\nthe function entry runs: that insert is behind an enclosing branch that is not taken.\n`class_instance_fields` is a RED HERRING — it is empty even in registering contexts.\n**THE REAL PRIMARY MAP for field-access lowering** (top of register_class_metadata, comment\n\"Store field index mapping for field access lowering (instance fields only)\"):\n    field_index_map.insert(field.symbol_id, (type_id, field_index));\nIt is keyed by **field.symbol_id** — and the probes PROVED the same field carries different\nSymbolIds per context: spinPool = SymbolId(7750) in one access context, SymbolId(9260) in\nanother. Declaring context registers under ITS id; consumer looks up under a DRIFTED id.\nClassic cluster disease, now in field_index_map.\n**FIX TARGET:** make field_index_map resolvable by NAME — either (a) publish\n(class_name, field_name) -\u003e field_index from the SAME loop that populates field_index_map\n(that loop DOES run; my mistake was attaching to the dead cif insert), and fall back at the\nE0100 site; or (b) key a parallel map by (class_name, field_name) at insert. CAUTION:\n`field_index` here vs the GEP `idx` used elsewhere — index 0 is the reserved __type_id\nheader; VERIFY the consumer's expected index space before returning it (off-by-one = silent\nmemory corruption, worse than E0100). Verify with the Q6_K WIP compile + Llama coherence.\nWORKING TREE: registry + 4 probes in hir_to_mir.rs UNCOMMITTED on top of 19eae55b.\n**THE FIX THAT WORKED:** publish `(class_name, field_name) -\u003e field_index` to the global\nname-keyed registry FROM THE `field_index_map` LOOP (the loop that provably runs — traced 88\nexecutions), consume at the E0100 site. Key by NAME both levels; carry ONLY the u32\nfield_index (same index space as the primary lookup — verified, not assumed); TypeIds never\ntravel. Result: spinPool/instance-field E0100s GONE, including the early-ordering ones.\nAttempts 1-3 failed because: (1) field-by-name behind class-by-ID; (2) both-by-name against\na map that was EMPTY (class_instance_fields is a red herring — its insert never fires); (3)\npublishing from that dead insert site.\n**STATICS RESIDUE:** `Q4Matmul.dumpCensus()` (zero-arg static) from the ENTRY module still\nE0100s when Q4Matmul.hx is edited — BOTH fully-qualified and import+unqualified forms.\nKEY CLUE: cross-module statics WITH ARGS resolve fine (Linear -\u003e Q4Matmul.matmul compiles\nand runs after the fix; nue.Linear was failing before it). So the statics flavor is either\nzero-arg-specific or entry-module-specific. The call falls through the method-call path into\nFIELD-ACCESS lowering (that is where the E0100 fires). Census exit-print in llama-chat\nMain.hx is commented with a TODO(compiler) until fixed — census COUNTING is unaffected.\nCOMPILER FIX (working tree, hir_to_mir.rs, UNCOMMITTED on top of 19eae55b): global\nname-keyed CLASS_FIELD_LAYOUTS registry + record_class_field() published from the\nfield_index_map loop + E0100-site fallback. **VERIFIED: instance-field E0100s (spinPool)\nGONE — Q6_K WIP now compiles.** Keep this; it is the E fix that worked.\nREMAINING exit=133 causes in the Q6_K WIP (/tmp/Q4Matmul.q6k-capture-wip.hx, updated):\n 1. My bsums-\u003ebsAddr rename hit ALL 32 MA4 call sites but `var bsAddr = bsums.address()` is\n    hoisted ONLY at :725 (runBanded). **runBandedFused (:1043) and matmulFused (:982) call\n    sites reference bsAddr with NO definition** -\u003e nue.Q4Matmul \"1 error\" -\u003e trap stub -\u003e\n    SIGTRAP. FIX: hoist per-function from THAT function's Bytes local (careful: the batch\n    fused path's local is `bsumsB`, not `bsums`).\n 2. UNVERIFIED RISK: new **E0803 \"ambiguous field access: headDim/name exists on multiple\n    classes\"** errors seen in full3.log (GGUF loader region; nue.Linear/BertArch each \"1\n    error\"). MUST determine whether MY registry fallback introduced these (a name-keyed\n    global registry can make a previously-failing lookup now AMBIGUOUS or wrongly matched\n    across same-named classes in different packages — the registry key is the UNQUALIFIED\n    class name!) or they are pre-existing. **CRITICAL SAFETY CHECK FIRST next session:\n    `git stash` the Q4Matmul WIP and run the COMMITTED tree with the new compiler — if plain\n    builds now emit E0803 or misbehave, the registry needs qualified-name keys before\n    anything else.** Llama + Qwen coherence must also be re-verified (registry returns an\n    index for ANY same-named class — unqualified-name collisions = silent wrong-GEP risk).\nMain.hx: census exit-print commented (TODO(compiler) zero-arg entry-module static);\ncopy at /tmp/Main.census-deferred.hx.\nThe name-keyed CLASS_FIELD_LAYOUTS registry SHIPPED: published from the field_index_map\nloop, consulted at the access site before erroring; only the u32 field_index travels.\nVERIFIED BOTH DIRECTIONS: the Q6_K capture-set edit that reproducibly broke unrelated\nmodules now compiles + runs (91.8 tok/s coherent), and the unmodified tree builds both\nQwen (74.6) and Llama (69.2) with ZERO E0100/E0803 under the new compiler. The E0803\nambiguity noise was cascade from the broken-module state, not the registry.\nRoot cause (for the record): imports forward a TYPE STUB into the consumer's type_table\n(class name + Class{symbol_id} resolve) but the FIELD LAYOUT only materialises when the\ndeclaring module's own pass runs register_class_metadata — any access lowered in the gap\nfailed, and editing Q4Matmul.hx perturbed lowering order enough to move accesses into it.\nOPEN follow-ups: (1) qualify registry keys (unqualified class names = cross-package\ncollision risk -\u003e silent wrong GEP; current tree verified collision-free); (2) statics\nflavor (zero-arg x-module static from ENTRY module; args-carrying statics fine) — census\nexit-print in llama-chat Main.hx deferred behind TODO(compiler); (3) rested A/B of the\nfull Haxe stack (single run 91.8 vs pre-fix 86.3 rested / Rust ~96) then consider flipping\nNUE_HAXE_Q8_0 default ON.\nCanonical (qualified) keys + bare-name alias map with POISONING: a second distinct\ncanonical class claiming a bare name poisons the alias; bare lookups then refuse -\u003e\nloud E0100, never first-writer-wins wrong GEP. Consumer tries qualified first, bare via\nalias second; both producer/consumer qualification asymmetries handled. Dead unqualified\npublisher deleted. Verified Qwen+Llama errs=0.\n\nRepro: zero-arg x-module static from the ENTRY module (`Q4Matmul.dumpCensus()` in\nllama-chat Main.hx, currently commented w/ TODO(compiler)). Statics WITH args resolve\n(Linear -\u003e Q4Matmul.matmul works). Earlier probe output shows the shape:\n  field='dumpCensus' sym=SymbolId(6293) receiver_ty=TypeId(907)\n    kind=Some(\"Class { symbol_id: SymbolId(6276) }\")\ni.e. the call falls out of METHOD-CALL lowering into FIELD-ACCESS lowering with the CLASS\nTYPE as receiver. The layout registry cannot help — it holds instance fields (GEP indices);\na static method needs a FUNCTION resolution, and the field-access site returns a\n(TypeId,u32,TypeId) GEP triple, so the fix does NOT belong there. FIX DIRECTION: find where\nstatic-method-call lowering misses (SymbolId-keyed fn lookup drifts) and falls through to\nfield access; add a name-keyed fallback THERE via external_function_name_map\n(`\u003cqualified\u003e.\u003cmethod\u003e` — the same mechanism the interface fat-ptr fix uses). The zero-arg\nvs with-args asymmetry suggests the with-args path already has param-count name matching\n(find_by_name_and_params) and the zero-arg path lacks it.\nZero-arg x-module static from the entry module resolved. Root cause: the Field-callee call\nchain had (1) resolve_function_id_with_qualified_fallback bailing on `?` when the drifted\nstub has NO qualified_name, (2) resolve_method_function_id missing when the class's methods\nwere never registered in that context; with-args statics survived via the param-count name\npaths, zero-arg had NO name route and fell into field-access lowering (static method has no\nGEP). FIX: third fallback constructing the EXACT `\u003cclass-qual|bare\u003e.\u003cmethod\u003e` key from the\ncallee Field's CLASS symbol -\u003e external_function_name_map + qualified-name scan. Exact-FQN,\nno suffix matching, only on the failing path.\nVERIFIED shipped default path: Qwen `Q8_0 haxe=30450 ffi=0, total ffi=0 (PURE HAXE)` 90.4\ntok/s; Llama `Q4_K_M haxe=20082 ffi=0 (PURE HAXE)` 72.5. clippy clean.\n**All three drift flavors from this session now closed by one principle: resolve x-module\nrefs by NAME with EXACT keys; fail loudly on a miss.** (20350f1e fields, ca776630\nhardening, 699af37f statics.)\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_xmodule_resolution_disease_cluster` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}